  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Now back to the tree."
   ],
   [
    1.471,
    "Inside the trunk are narrow tubes, and a column of water fills each one from the roots to the leaves."
   ],
   [
    8.398,
    "At the leaves, water evaporates into the air."
   ],
   [
    11.68,
    "Each molecule that leaves tugs on the one below it, and because of cohesion, the whole chain follows, like a rope being drawn up."
   ],
   [
    20.0,
    "The tube walls help too."
   ],
   [
    21.51,
    "Water also sticks to other materials, here the wall, through hydrogen bonds."
   ],
   [
    26.458,
    "That is adhesion, and it keeps the column from sliding back down."
   ],
   [
    30.417,
    "So gravity pulls down, but evaporation pulls up, cohesion links the chain, and adhesion grips the wall."
   ]
  ]
 },
