  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Why is water so stubborn?"
   ],
   [
    1.862,
    "When heat flows in, a large share goes into breaking hydrogen bonds."
   ],
   [
    6.536,
    "Energy spent snapping bonds is energy that does not speed the molecules up, so the temperature climbs slowly."
   ],
   [
    13.711,
    "When water cools, bonds form again, and they release that energy as heat."
   ],
   [
    18.698,
    "So water soaks up heat slowly and gives it back slowly, and its temperature swings less."
   ]
  ]
 },
